  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Remind me to check up on 貰う etc. with all that in-group / out-group etc stuff.",
      "html": "Remind me to check up on 貰う etc. with all that in-group / out-group etc stuff.",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "a64a3bf5de03f141779c66172c560da6d9d02e036079f9c8bdd331e31df2a7c5",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "に marks the indirect object of the verb\nreceiver of the action",
      "html": "に marks the indirect object of the verb<br/>receiver of the action",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "2581806e0b86f251d80bb25144a24839c261aecef4db7a10f6914db63d30a227",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Some E translations don't have right words just for に and I put verb instead. Please change English if you have better translation.",
      "html": "Some E translations don't have right words just for に and I put verb instead. Please change English if you have better translation.",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "217278831cd3b49cf03576143919f86ac1b503561bcd28612420176aa5ab121d",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "there is a mistake in the grammar in #4899\nshould be something like \"please let me know when you get there.\"",
      "html": "there is a mistake in the grammar in #4899<br/>should be something like \"please let me know when you get there.\"",
      "credits_raw": "ck1984",
      "content_sha256": "3c208e9211a1481451646eaa2618779d3ae38c79be8de7ff50237518ba641e76",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "\"に marks the indirect object of the verb\nreceiver of the action\"\n\nthis causes some confusion with ex #4902 since 'he' is the one receiving the scolding?",
      "html": "\"に marks the indirect object of the verb<br/>receiver of the action\"<br/><br/>this causes some confusion with ex #4902 since 'he' is the one receiving the scolding?",
      "credits_raw": "skysongz",
      "content_sha256": "66d4a195acd200225a9e98f28fd0ab804469ab633a90ab7914800a950eafa393",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I was a bit confused about this as well, though thinking of it as marking an indirect object helps so much-- all of the books and things have explained it in a way that connects it to its first meaning...",
      "html": "I was a bit confused about this as well, though thinking of it as marking an indirect object helps so much-- all of the books and things have explained it in a way that connects it to its first meaning...",
      "credits_raw": "Saralynne",
      "content_sha256": "97cbc5a8d81526081bc0259860d3b72d286ded5bd53f1bf8854dc99b22f04148",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Isn't the verb in #4902 in passive form? If that's the case, then に denotes the agent (I think that's the correct English term) of the action. In other words, the one acting/subject.\n\nThat's why the English translation is in passive form also. I think.",
      "html": "Isn't the verb in #4902 in passive form? If that's the case, then に denotes the agent (I think that's the correct English term) of the action. In other words, the one acting/subject.<br/><br/>That's why the English translation is in passive form also. I think.",
      "credits_raw": "yari",
      "content_sha256": "8b19d0b618ce9b8747af179b35c6d201c536096775cebab38dff2c261bb5c2eb",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    }
